I wrote the session plan: two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The commit failed because session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so nothing was committed. The planning prompt's commit command ends in || true, so the harness doesn't expect that commit to succeed, and the files are on disk where the next phase reads them.

Task 1 — Part of #1041 (product): a stdio MCP server that exposes a tool named like one of yoyo's own is currently skipped whole. The flagship filesystem server is one, so its users get none of its tools. This task connects such a server with all its tools renamed under a prefix instead.
• The decisions are made in the task file so the implementer doesn't spend the slot on design:
  • The prefix only applies to servers that clash; other servers connect exactly as today.
  • A configured server uses its [mcp_servers.<name>] name as the prefix; a --mcp server gets mcpN.
  • If the prefixed names still clash, the server is skipped as before.
  • HTTP servers aren't covered, which is why the title says "Part of".
• All the new logic goes in a new src/mcp_prefix.rs, because agent_builder.rs is only about 40 lines from the module-size limit, and crossing it would revert the whole task.
• Tests plus one deliberate break-and-restore run, and a CLAUDE.md update that keeps the old "skipped" claim as superseded.

Task 2 — Fixes #1042 (product): after /cd, /spawn reloads the new directory's instruction files but only checks them against the startup deny list, so a file denied by the /cd list can still reach the sub-agent's prompt. This is read from code, not yet reproduced on the binary.
• The test that should fail goes in first, using the existing test-only entry point rather than the global deny list.
• The loader then switches to the same /cd-aware check the other file doors already use.
• src/context.rs comes off the list of unfixed readers, so that count drops by exactly one.

